3. Use it from ActualiteModal.tsx

For example, your state:

const [paragraphe, setParagraphe] = useState("");

Then:

<RichTextEditor
  value={paragraphe}
  onChange={setParagraphe}
/>

Import it:

import RichTextEditor from "@/components/RichTextEditor/RichTextEditor";

Now whenever the user types or formats text:

Bonjour ceci est normal.

Ceci est BOLD.

Ceci est italic.

the parent automatically receives something like:

<p>Bonjour ceci est normal.</p>
<div>
  Ceci est <b>BOLD</b>.
</div>
<div>
  Ceci est <i>italic</i>.
</div>

So when you submit your form:

const handleSubmit = () => {
  console.log(paragraphe);

  // Send to .NET API
  // paragraphe contains the formatted HTML
};

The important idea

Your component works like this:

ActualiteModal
      │
      │ value
      ▼
RichTextEditor
      │
      │ onChange(html)
      ▼
ActualiteModal
      │
      ▼
.NET API
      │
      ▼
Oracle

So you don't need to access the editor with a ref from the parent. The parent simply owns the paragraphe value.

For your existing Actualités CRUD, this means your database Paragraphe column can contain the formatted HTML while Titre, Description, Catégorie, etc. remain normal fields.